---
// The sowing-time example's fuller results, read from result.extra in E1's
// JSON. A block whose numbers are absent is left out and named in the build log.
import { num, range, withRange, count, pct } from "../data/format";
interface Props { x: Record<string, any> }
const { x } = Astro.props;
const has = (block: string, keys: string[]) => {
  const miss = keys.filter((k) => x[k] === undefined || x[k] === null);
  if (miss.length) console.warn(`[E1] result.extra lacks ${miss.join(", ")}: the "${block}" block is left out.`);
  return miss.length === 0;
};
const v = (k: string) => x[k] as number[];
const cell = (k: string) => (Array.isArray(x[k]) ? withRange(x[k][0], x[k][1], x[k][2]) : "not estimated");
const iv = (k: string) => range(v(k)[1], v(k)[2]);
const usd = (n: number) => `$${Math.round(n).toLocaleString("en-AU")}`;
const includesZero = (k: string) => Array.isArray(x[k]) && x[k][1] <= 0 && x[k][2] >= 0;
const width = (k: string) => (Array.isArray(x[k]) ? x[k][2] - x[k][1] : NaN);
const overlaps = (a: string, b: string) => Array.isArray(x[a]) && Array.isArray(x[b]) && x[a][1] <= x[b][2] && x[b][1] <= x[a][2];

const showDesign = has("pairs", ["n_pairs", "n_sites", "year_min", "year_max", "gap_min_days", "gap_max_days", "gap_median_days", "n_variety_pairs", "n_varieties"]);
const showBalance = has("balance", ["kernr_p_primary", "kernr_p_with_rain", "rain_early_mm", "rain_main_mm"]);
const showThree = has("three numbers", ["asreml_ate", "fb_ate", "mean_main_yield", "value_ate_aud_ha", "price_aud_t", "price_low_aud_t", "price_high_aud_t", "p_gain", "p_gain_new_paddock", "decider_value_new_paddock_aud_ha"]);
const tableKeys = ["n_pairs", "n_pairs_south", "n_pairs_north", "n_pairs_same_week", "asreml_ate", "asreml_south", "asreml_north", "asreml_same_week", "fb_ate", "fb_south", "fb_north", "fb_same_week", "pm_ate", "pm_south", "pm_north", "apsim_ate", "apsim_south", "apsim_north"];
const showTable = has("estimates table", tableKeys);
const showN = has("nitrogen by sowing day", ["n_total_early", "n_sow_early", "n_total_main", "n_sow_main"]);
const showLimits = has("what it does not show", ["lost_candidates", "lost_early_only", "lost_main_only", "lost_both", "asreml_same_week"]);
const rows = [
  { label: "All pairs", n: "n_pairs", s: "ate" },
  { label: "Southern NSW", n: "n_pairs_south", s: "south" },
  { label: "North", n: "n_pairs_north", s: "north" },
];
---
{showDesign && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">The pairs</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    <li>The pairs were fixed before any yield was read: {count(x.n_pairs)} pairs at {count(x.n_sites)} sites in NSW and
      Queensland, {x.year_min} to {x.year_max}, sown {count(x.gap_min_days)} to {count(x.gap_max_days)} days apart
      (median {count(x.gap_median_days)}).</li>
    <li>They give {count(x.n_variety_pairs)} Early-minus-Main differences across {count(x.n_varieties)} varieties.</li>
    <li>Sites are split into southern NSW and the north (northern NSW and Queensland) at 31.5° S.</li>
  </ul>
</>}

{showBalance && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">Did the trials match before sowing?</h2>
  <p class="prose">kernR compared Early and Main trials on soil (clay, pH, water-holding capacity) and on the nitrogen
    applied on or before the sowing day, all at once (permutation p = {num(x.kernr_p_primary)}). The month before sowing
    averaged {num(x.rain_early_mm)} mm of rain for Early trials and {num(x.rain_main_mm)} mm for Main trials. With rainfall
    added, the test gives p = {num(x.kernr_p_with_rain)}.</p>
</>}

{showThree && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">Three numbers</h2>
  <div class="studies grid grid-3">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="kicker">The average gain</p>
      <h3>{num(v("asreml_ate")[0])} t/ha ({iv("asreml_ate")})</h3>
      <p class="mt-1">On the same paddock and in the same season, the same variety yielded {num(v("asreml_ate")[0])} t/ha
        more sown in the Early window (ASReml), against a mean Main-window yield of {num(x.mean_main_yield)} t/ha.
        flexyBayes gives {num(v("fb_ate")[0])}{Array.isArray(x.pm_ate) && <> and proxymix {num(v("pm_ate")[0])}</>}.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="kicker">What it is worth</p>
      <h3>{usd(v("value_ate_aud_ha")[0])}/ha ({usd(v("value_ate_aud_ha")[1])} to {usd(v("value_ate_aud_ha")[2])})</h3>
      <p class="mt-1">The flexyBayes gain valued at {usd(x.price_aud_t)}/t, the ABARES wheat gross unit value averaged
        over the study seasons ({usd(x.price_low_aud_t)} to {usd(x.price_high_aud_t)}/t across them), with early sowing
        taken to cost nothing extra. The range covers yield uncertainty only. The chance that the average gain is
        positive is {pct(x.p_gain)}.{x.decider_choice && <> decideR chooses the {x.decider_choice} window.</>}</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="kicker">On any one paddock</p>
      <h3>{pct(x.p_gain_new_paddock)} chance of a gain</h3>
      <p class="mt-1">The gain varies between sites and seasons. On a new paddock and season, decideR puts the expected
        value of sowing early at {usd(x.decider_value_new_paddock_aud_ha)}/ha.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</>}

{showTable && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">The estimates</h2>
  <p class="prose">Early minus Main yield, t/ha, with the 90 per cent interval in brackets: a confidence interval for
    ASReml, a credible interval for flexyBayes, a bootstrap interval for proxymix and the spread of the calibrated
    simulations for APSIM.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll mt-1" tabindex="0">
    <table class="num">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Pairs</th><th scope="col">n</th><th scope="col">ASReml</th><th scope="col">flexyBayes</th><th scope="col">proxymix</th><th scope="col">APSIM with PESTO</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <tr><th scope="row">{r.label}</th><td>{count(x[r.n])}</td><td>{cell(`asreml_${r.s}`)}</td><td>{cell(`fb_${r.s}`)}</td><td>{cell(`pm_${r.s}`)}</td><td>{cell(`apsim_${r.s}`)}</td></tr>
        ))}
        <tr><th scope="row">Sown under a week apart</th><td>{count(x.n_pairs_same_week)}</td><td>{cell("asreml_same_week")}</td><td>{cell("fb_same_week")}</td><td>not estimated</td><td>not estimated</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <ul class="prose mt-2">
    <li>In the north the ASReml and flexyBayes intervals {includesZero("asreml_north") && includesZero("fb_north")
      ? "include zero, so a gain there is not established" : "exclude zero"}. In southern NSW they{" "}
      {includesZero("asreml_south") || includesZero("fb_south") ? "include zero" : "exclude zero"}.</li>
    <li>APSIM, calibrated with PESTO, expected {v("apsim_ate")[0] < v("asreml_ate")[0] ? "less" : "more"} than the trials
      show. The ASReml and APSIM intervals {overlaps("asreml_ate", "apsim_ate") ? "overlap" : "do not overlap"}.</li>
    {width("pm_ate") < width("asreml_ate") && <li>proxymix's interval is narrower than the mixed models'. It does not
      carry the variation between sites and seasons that the mixed models include.</li>}
  </ul>
</>}

{showN && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">Nitrogen applied by sowing day</h2>
  <p class="prose">Part of the nitrogen applied to these trials goes on after sowing, as an in-crop top-dressing. On
    average, Early trials received {num(x.n_total_early)} kg N/ha, of which {num(x.n_sow_early)} was applied on or before
    the sowing day; Main trials received {num(x.n_total_main)}, of which {num(x.n_sow_main)}. How much nitrogen goes on
    in-crop can depend on how the crop looks, and so on when it was sown, so it cannot be used to check that the trials
    matched before sowing. The balance check and the proxymix covariates use only the nitrogen applied on or before the
    sowing day. The ASReml and flexyBayes estimates use no covariates.</p>
</>}

{showLimits && <>
  <h2 class="mt-4">What it does not show</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    <li><strong>Trials with no yields.</strong> A trial with no yields in the data cannot be paired, and the data do not
      say why. Of {count(x.lost_candidates)} same-paddock pairs sown a week or more apart, {count(x.lost_early_only)} lost
      only the Early trial's yields, {count(x.lost_main_only)} only the Main trial's and {count(x.lost_both)} both. If
      those crops failed, leaving them out changes the average, and no adjustment removes that.</li>
    <li><strong>More than sowing date.</strong> Pairs sown under a week apart differed by {cell("asreml_same_week")} t/ha,
      so part of the gap may come from the trial series rather than the sowing date. These pairs sit at different sites
      from the rest, so the figure is reported beside the main estimate and not subtracted from it.</li>
    <li><strong>Where on the paddock.</strong> In the causal graph of the design (Hernán and Robins 2020), a pair shares
      site, season and variety, so comparing within it adjusts for them. The estimate assumes the Early trials were not
      sown on a better or worse part of the paddock than the Main trials.</li>
    <li><strong>The price.</strong> The value assumes early sowing costs nothing extra and uses the average price of the
      study seasons, not a forecast.</li>
  </ul>
</>}
